<title>THAILAND: Thai phone agency seeks 16.5 bln baht ADB loan.</title>
<headline>Thai phone agency seeks 16.5 bln baht ADB loan.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Telephone Organisation of Thailand (TOT) was seeking 16.5 billion baht in loans (US$660 million) from the Asian Development Bank (ADB) to invest in its rural public telephone projects, a senior official said on Friday.</p>
<p>The project was started this year and would be completed in 1998, Sirin Thoopklam, TOT chairman of the board, told reporters.</p>
<p>TOT and the finance ministry will negotiate the details of the loan with ADB if and when it was approved, he said.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
